---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_130",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 130,
  "text": "<p> [[367.3]] <b>116. LEIBNIZ AN PIERRE DANIEL HUET</p>\n<p> [[367.4]] [Paris,] 10. Mai 1673. [115.185a.]</b></p>\n<p> [[367.28]] Illustri Viro D. Petro Danieli Huetio </p>\n<p> [[367.29]] S.P.D. Gottfredus Guilielmus Leibnitius. </p>\n<p> [[367.30]] Pro certo comperi Vitruvium celeberrimi Valesii sub praelo sudare: editore nobis multa\n[[367.31]] nova ac singularia a se primum detecta, promittente, in quibus omnes hactenus interpretes\n[[368.1]] lapsi sint, eosque errores per totum Vitruvium fusos esse. Quae res facit, ut antequam editio ista\n[[368.2]] prodeat, manum admoliri scriptori non ausim, ac ne constituere quidem mecum, quid Tibi\n[[368.3]] promittere debeam, praeterquam enim, quod vir tantus fortasse hominem novum in occupatam\n[[368.4]] a se materiam involare non satis aequo animo laturus sit, paratus ipse succum Gallicae editionis\n[[368.5]] Latina complecti, ut quemadmodum illic Colberto, ita hic Montauserio, utrobique Regi satisfaciat;\n[[368.6]] superest et aliud cogitandum mihi, an nimirum post messem ejus spicilegium mihi\n[[368.7]] relictum sit, observationum quarundam non contemnendarum. Ita enim ego animatus sum, ut ne\n[[368.8]] attingere quidem argumentum audeam, ubi spes non sit praestari aliquid extra ordinem posse,\n[[368.9]] nam medullam bonorum interpretum clare breviterque exhibere, fortasse non adeo difficile\n[[368.10]] fuerit. Quare venia Tua, Vir Amplissime, eousque deliberationem meam differre cogor, nisi\n[[368.11]] quis interim, aptior me, in tanta praestantium virorum copia, eam operam occupaverit. </p>\n<p> [[368.12]] Ac fortasse interea, nisi Tibi aliter videtur, Martianum absolvero, cum disciplinae quas\n[[368.13]] tractat ille, magis in medio positae, novo quodam apparatu tantopere non indigeant: at qui\n[[368.14]] Vitruvium pro argumenti dignitate tractare velit, eum ad nostri temporis experimenta respicere,\n[[368.15]] et cum opificibus atque architectis conferre debere censeo: ut collatis veterum praeceptis, et\n[[368.16]] peritia nostrorum, aliquid inde usus in publicum dimanet. Sed haec tempus otiumque huic uni\n[[368.17]] rei aliquandiu impensum postulant. </p>\n<p> [[368.18]] Ad Martianum vero sunt mihi jam in promtu nova quaedam ac forsan digna scitu,\n[[368.19]] plerisque artibus quas ille tractat, nonnihil illustrandis; quae et publici magis saporis sunt,\n[[368.20]] juvenique, quali laboratur congruentiora. Cum Vitruviana non nisi ab artificibus, aut aliis\n[[368.21]] quidem, sed in severiorum disciplinarum cultu profectis, intelligantur. Adde quod Capella a\n[[368.22]] nemine perpetuo commentario illustratus est, et, si quis alius Veterum, remedio ab Ill^#'m^#'o Duce\n[[368.23]] Montauserio invento, id est versione, ut sic dicam Latina, indiget. </p>\n<p> [[368.24]] Mitto ecce specimen in Martianum, idem illud, quod jam monstraveram, sed reformatum.\n[[368.25]] Ex intertexta enim explicatione continuam velut versionem feci. Notae sunt tumultuariae;\n[[368.26]] scriptae scilicet, nullo alio libro adhibito, praeterquam ipso Martiano: postea polientur. Cavi ne\n[[368.27]] a Grotio dicta repeterem, cujus notas, nisi aliter sentis, integras inserere cogito. Mitto et\n[[368.28]] <i>Argumentum totius fabulae</i>, quod inter legendum memoriae causa ludens contexui. Haec a Te\n[[368.29]] coram, ubi permiseris, recepero. </p>\n<p> [[369.1]] Nisi interrumpar solito frequentius, faxo ne moram meam accusetis et interrumpor sane\n[[369.2]] non raro, cum demonstrationes quasdam in Arithmetica tum simplici, tum infinitorum, et\n[[369.3]] Geometria, et Scientia motus, et Optica, et Mechanicis, a me repertas, poliri ac publicari amici\n[[369.4]] flagitent. Nec negligendum est commercium literarium, cum amicis in Germania, Anglia,\n[[369.5]] Septentrione. Nuper ut obiter dicam, misere mihi ex [Anglia], rationem Corporis Algebraici\n[[369.6]] condendi, quod moliuntur absolutissimum certe, congestis in unum omnibus omnium, quae\n[[369.7]] hactenus in eo argumento extant, inventis. Sed et Machina Arithmetica me subinde sibi\n[[369.8]] vendicat, quae nunc properat ad metam, specimen fortasse datura, posse a machinis effici, quae\n[[369.9]] hominis etiam industrii non manum tantum, sed et ingenium fatigant. </p>\n<p> [[369.10]] Haec spero, Vir Ampl^#'m^#'e, excusabunt me apud Te, si assiduitatem praestare semper non\n[[369.11]] possum; et hodie certe venire me, ut erat officii mei, mutatio domicilii, quod nunc in S. Germani\n[[369.12]] suburbium, ac Palatii Luxemburgici viciniam transfero, prohibet: dissolvendis componendisque\n[[369.13]] reculis occupatum. Spero habiturum me occasionem, nisi statim San Germanum\n[[369.14]] redis, excusandi me coram. </p>\n<p> [[369.15]] Interea vale ac homini Tibi obsequentissimo fave. </p>\n",
  "number": "116.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN PIERRE DANIEL HUET",
  "date": "[Paris,] 10. Mai 1673. [115.185a.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:116. LEIBNIZ AN PIERRE DANIEL HUET [Paris,] 10. Mai 1673. [115.185a.] Illustri Viro D. Petro Danieli Huetio S.P.D. Gottfredus Guilielmus Leibnitius. Pro certo comperi Vitruvium celeberrimi Valesii sub praelo sudare: editore nobis multa nova ac singularia a se primum detecta, promittente, in quibus o...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>